validate/effective_size.jl impact — what ne = :breeders (N_e = the breeders) changes, against the default ne = :falconer
Only functions that call effective_size are affected: house_of_gauss_vg/_G and house_of_cards_vg when nsurv < PopSize is passed, and
drift_critical_rate. The moments lowering (run_moments, multilocus_equilibrium, emulate, half_survival_rate's survival) uses the parents n directly.

